WEBVTT

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:19.820
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:19.820
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:19.820
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:47.600
Dreams of the Morning, Songs of the Night

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:47.600
Chapter 3

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.780
I'm sorry about this
unfortunate accident.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:15.220
They told the family and school-related
people that it was an accident, right ?

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.200
For now.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.750
Not to borrow the principal's words,
but the rumor will eventually spread.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.950
Do you think that the
perpetrator is here ?

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:30.570
Rather, it's hard to think
that an outsider did this.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.840
I can't think of anyone other
than school-related people.{who would do this}

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.430
True.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.010
The class representative,
Moritz von Haase.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:27.660
I will do my best to bid farewell
to our friend, Karl von Reifeisen.

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:34.470
Your sudden death was a
shock to everyone in the class.

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:32.110
That guy is making
the memorial address.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.470
He is at the top of the class.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.660
You were always full
of energy and aspirations.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:40.250
When we had to pull all-nighters
before exams, you always said...

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.150
"My health is the
only thing I'm good at."

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:45.900
Just like you said, you
were tougher than anyone...

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:50.770
...and it is unbelievable that
you could end up like this.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:54.340
It's a perfect address,
but his heart isn't in it.

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:56.800
Although we are here
for your funeral...

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:55.800
Lord Reinhard.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.820
...it still feels like you will
one day return in good health.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:05.900
Come to think of it, you were the
closest friend I had in this class.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:08.840
It's somewhat strange that
we got along so well...

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.700
...having totally different
personalities and backgrounds...

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.970
...but I always loved
how energetic you were.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:21.720
You always received good grades,
and you were my rival academically.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:26.750
But you were an invaluable friend, who,
as a student of this military school...

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:34.150
...would have eventually fought with
us against the enemies of the Reich.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:39.400
I'm sorry that this unfortunate accident
took your life so close to our graduation...

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:45.950
...and so close to reaching the
dream of fighting on the battlefield.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:55.250
It is a great loss to the Reich,
and we can't regret this enough.

00:04:55.250 --> 00:05:02.100
We, as your classmates, pledge that we
will do our best to carry on your will.

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:01.930
After the memorial address, the women
attending the funeral will start crying.

00:05:03.130 --> 00:05:10.250
I hope that Karl von Reifeisen's
soul will rest in peace.

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.350
It's a total formality.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:05.940
Captain.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.410
{You must be 
}I'm sorry about the
accident, Captain Reifeisen.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.100
You must be Captain Musel.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.470
I've heard the story.

00:06:20.210 --> 00:06:21.580
Thank you.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:31.020
Please find the perpetrator and
punish him accordingly for his crime.

00:06:31.610 --> 00:06:32.980
Of course.

00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:36.110
I will do my best to make the
perpetrator pay for your son's death.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:41.200
Thank you.
Please take care of it.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:43.130
I surely will.

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:47.030
It's hard for me
to say this to you...

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:51.330
...but please do not announce
that your son was murdered.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.360
I understand.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:57.540
It has to do with the honor of the
Empire and the military school.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.290
What's wrong,
Lord Reinhard ?

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:14.690
I don't like it.

00:07:14.690 --> 00:07:20.410
How obedient Captain Reifeisen is, and
that I'm in the position to ask him for it.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:26.660
The tolerance of the ruled...

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:31.240
...allows the ruler to grow imprudent,
and loosens the ruler's concentration.

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:36.800
What you're saying is right, but in
this situation, it's hard to blame him.

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:40.260
You're right.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:42.270
It's not his fault.

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.250
People's minds have been
enslaved for 5 centuries...

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:48.280
...no, more like
made into livestock.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:50.150
He is a victim.

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:51.420
We shouldn't blame him.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.220
But...

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.220
...I will not agree that the
victimization is one sided.

00:08:30.710 --> 00:08:31.950
Something is bothering me.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:35.790
But I don't
know what it is.

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:38.500
It feels as if some food has
gotten stuck in my back teeth.

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:41.790
That must be annoying.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:52.930
But we only have one week, so we
should concentrate on the investigation.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.110
We wasted some time
with this funeral...

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:59.220
...but things like this
shouldn't happen too often.

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:05.960
But Reinhard's prediction was wrong in an unexpected way.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:30.870
This is Siefrin
Imperial Hospital.

00:09:31.580 --> 00:09:35.770
Is this Imperial
Captain Reinhard von Musel ?

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:36.710
Yes.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:39.250
Your father...

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:48.800
...<i>Reichsleiter</i> Sebastian von Musel passed away
on April 28 at 19:40, Imperial Year 484...

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:51.600
...in the intensive care
unit of this hospital.

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.250
The cause of his death
was cirrhosis of the liver.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:05.870
We did our best to treat him but it was
too late when he arrived at the hospital.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:13.950
I am really sorry, but he did not stop
drinking until he was hospitalized.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:19.110
I am aware that he had problems
with managing his own health...

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:21.790
...and that this is no
fault of the hospital.

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:23.460
I understand the situation.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:25.270
Thank you.

00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:27.440
Then...

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:43.290
Don't worry, Kircheis.

00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:44.850
I will attend the funeral.

00:10:48.270 --> 00:10:50.200
If I don't, my sister
will scold me.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:03.600
Lord Reinhard.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.900
You sold my sister !

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:15.090
Reinhard.

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:24.760
It's an honor for Annerose
to go to the royal palace.

00:11:25.690 --> 00:11:28.810
This money is for
the preparations.

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:32.630
No matter how you say it,
the fact is you sold my sister !

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:33.520
Reinhard.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:38.450
We can't refuse the Kaiser.

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:42.510
So we might as
well take the money.

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:54.590
Lord Reinhard
hated Mr. Sebastian.

00:11:55.210 --> 00:12:02.250
Just like the Kaiser, the nobility,
and the society that supports them.

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:04.500
They are accomplices.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:10.690
I see.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:18.250
The ones that support and submit to
them are the ones Lord Reinhard hates...

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:19.680
...and are the ones
he wants to change.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:49.140
Of course, it's
not a family grave.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:54.820
It's a grave my sister
acquired for my mother.

00:12:54.820 --> 00:13:00.100
He not only drank away the "preparation money,"
he also drank away his pension.

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.940
He had no fortune left.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:05.720
He doesn't have the
right to be in that tomb.

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:14.110
Those who attended the funeral
mostly want my sister's attention.

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:16.520
No one really mourns
for him in their heart.

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:20.580
Lady Annerose does, at least.

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:23.280
Did you hear about this ?

00:13:23.970 --> 00:13:28.230
He turned down
the title of baron.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.930
No, I heard it's the opposite.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:35.290
He asked for a
barony, but was denied.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.480
Oh, now that I can believe.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:42.440
I've heard both rumors.

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:46.280
Reinhard probably believes
the latter unconditionally.

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:50.280
If he did turn down the
offer to become a baron...

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:54.900
...was it his way to
take the responsibility ?

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:11.850
There are thousands of people who've sold
their daughters to the Kaiser or the nobility.

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:15.970
But why does
Reinhard blame me ?

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:26.040
Kircheis.

00:14:26.750 --> 00:14:27.680
My sister...

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:43.700
Lady Annerose.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:45.590
Sieg.

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:47.350
Thank you for coming today.

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:50.320
Lady Annerose...

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:57.040
...if there are any problems at the palace,
please tell me or Lord Reinhard.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.260
We might be
able to comfort you.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.850
Thank you, Sieg.

00:15:03.550 --> 00:15:04.930
Thank you.

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:07.950
Countess Grunewald.

00:15:10.460 --> 00:15:17.850
I am really sorry about this but the Kaiser wants you to attend the opera tonight.

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:22.400
It starts at 7, so we
should head back and prepare.

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.050
Lord Reinhard.

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:21.150
Anyway...

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:26.850
...my sister and I
are half-way released.

00:16:28.110 --> 00:16:31.110
We should release the
other half by ourselves.

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:35.870
We will definitely
do it, Kircheis.

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:40.180
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:17:05.250 --> 00:17:06.250
What's wrong ?

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:08.630
There's been
another murder.

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:10.400
What ?

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:20.660
Who was the victim ?

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:23.360
Johann Gottholp von Bertz.

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:26.690
He was also a senior,
and second in the class.

00:17:29.760 --> 00:17:31.610
They've done it.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.290
And right in front of me.

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:38.100
The perpetrator did it when
you were away, Lord Reinhard.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:43.250
At any rate, it's my fault
that we couldn't prevent this.

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:45.500
It's this way.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.230
The dead body was
in the last stall...

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:16.080
...but the murder seems
to have occurred here.

00:18:16.870 --> 00:18:19.760
The perpetrator seemed to
put the body in the back...

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:22.470
...and tried to
clean up the evidence.

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:27.950
As you can see, blood on
the wall was cleaned up...

00:18:27.950 --> 00:18:29.970
...and there was also an attempt
to wipe the blood off the floor.

00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:32.070
It's strange.

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:33.200
Yes.

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.850
He didn't wipe the
floor all the way.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:39.910
It could be that he gave
up on it for some reason.

00:18:39.910 --> 00:18:43.090
For example, he didn't have
the time or someone came in.

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:47.610
But there is a trace that he wiped
places where there wasn't any blood.

00:18:47.610 --> 00:18:48.760
What ?

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:50.260
What's going on ?

00:18:54.760 --> 00:19:00.800
I'm disappointed that we could
not stop this with you here.

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:04.250
If you are talking about
taking responsibility...

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:06.600
...you have the biggest responsibility
as principal to manage this school.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:09.470
I'm disappointed as well.

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:13.520
Bertz wanted to
talk to me privately.

00:19:14.320 --> 00:19:18.800
Come to think of it, he must have found
the perpetrator or witnessed the crime...

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:23.220
...wanted to report to me,
and was killed because of it.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:27.930
It's likely, but why didn't
you tell me about it ?

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:31.210
I just realized it.

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:34.570
I didn't think anything
of it at the time.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:38.160
And I had other
worries as well.

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:55.650
I want to see what it was
like right after the incident.

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:56.660
Are there any photos of it ?

00:19:57.240 --> 00:20:00.030
There should be some
from the examiners.

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.250
Please wait for a moment.

00:20:07.300 --> 00:20:09.750
Huh ?
It happened again.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:10.420
What happened ?

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:11.550
I'm sorry.

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:12.730
This thing is old.

00:20:33.970 --> 00:20:37.140
I've figured out what
was nagging at me.

00:20:48.330 --> 00:20:52.790
Do you remember when we 
talked to Haase the first time ?

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:00.640
Which team scored ?

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:05.690
At that time, he answered,
"The team that's not yellow."

00:21:08.920 --> 00:21:11.850
He could have
said the red team.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:12.870
Yes.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:15.910
You or I would have
said it that way.

00:21:16.720 --> 00:21:19.930
But Haase couldn't.

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:22.220
He's colorblind ?

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:25.650
I had forgotten that term.

00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:29.710
He's probably
severely colorblind.

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:32.930
But he hid that fact and
entered military school.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:37.050
You think that secret is
the motive for the murder ?

00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:42.990
Since the time of Rudolf, colorblindness
has been considered genetically inferior.

00:21:42.990 --> 00:21:46.600
If this became known, it would
mean expulsion at the very least.

00:21:47.150 --> 00:21:49.620
Such a stupid rule.

00:21:49.620 --> 00:21:52.540
But it is surely
enough as a motive.

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:59.950
It would also explain why the blood on the
green tiles was not wiped up completely.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:08.900
Well, doesn't all the evidence point
to Moritz von Haase as the suspect ?

00:22:10.750 --> 00:22:15.180
There's just too much evidence
that leads to that conclusion.

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:16.490
What ?

00:22:17.310 --> 00:22:19.150
Something is bothering me.

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:20.030
Something...

00:22:23.960 --> 00:22:27.900
He figured out one of the
mysteries to solve the mystery.

00:22:28.900 --> 00:22:33.260
But Reinhard felt something that makes him
believe he hasn't found everything yet.

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:40.250
Now, Reinhard is experiencing how it
feels to have something nagging at him.

00:22:37.850 --> 00:22:41.450
To be continued

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:49.400
[ Long Relationship ]

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:49.400
Ending Theme

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:49.400
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:55.700
I don't wait to live a life of counting memories

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:56.250
Reinhard:

00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:56.250
Horikawa Ryo

00:22:57.240 --> 00:23:03.010
Steger:

00:22:57.240 --> 00:23:03.010
Fujimoto Yuzuru

00:22:57.250 --> 00:23:09.800
But with you, I've had a long relationship...

00:23:04.670 --> 00:23:10.590
Annerose:

00:23:04.670 --> 00:23:10.590
Han Keiko

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:17.550
Narrator:

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:17.550
Yara Yuusaku

00:23:11.750 --> 00:23:17.000
...and it feels as though the memories...

00:23:17.850 --> 00:23:24.670
...might get carried off somewhere

00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:24.070
Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:30.270
Timing:
Todd Perkins

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:31.050
Maybe it's a momentary worry

00:23:30.270 --> 00:23:36.280
Song Translation:
Toshiaki

00:23:31.750 --> 00:23:37.750
Thinking, "People change," I shake my head

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:42.280
Editing:
Todd Perkins
Barbara
Dave
Brain
Mouse
Steve S.
Horus

00:23:38.650 --> 00:23:48.300
The sunset sky and the stars laugh at such idiocy

00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:52.440
Subtitled by:
Central Anime(Kansas)

00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:15.500
A long relationship, that is just like the character "humans"

00:24:16.900 --> 00:24:23.000
They love and support...

00:24:23.800 --> 00:24:30.450
...while at the same time pursuing their own dreams

00:24:30.450 --> 00:24:35.350
And I feel that's okay

00:24:53.200 --> 00:24:58.190
Preview of Next Episode

00:24:55.770 --> 00:24:59.250
All the evidence pointed
to Haase as the perpetrator.

00:24:59.250 --> 00:25:02.420
But Reinhard questions the fact
that there is so much evidence.

00:25:02.420 --> 00:25:05.540
There is too much
circumstantial evidence.

00:25:05.540 --> 00:25:07.680
He figures out the
meaning behind this...

00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:11.240
...and he sets a trap to ferret
out the real perpetrator.

00:25:12.700 --> 00:25:14.600
Next episode of...

00:25:13.280 --> 00:25:23.290
Legend of the Galactic Heroes Gaiden

00:25:13.280 --> 00:25:23.290
Dreams of the Morning, Songs of the Night
Chapter 4

00:25:18.750 --> 00:25:22.250
Within the galaxy, there are stories that have not been told yet.
